  formula: ChatzosHalayla
  description: "Chatzos halayla.\n\nFor how chatzos can be defined and calculated, see [The Definition of Chatzos](https://kosherjava.com/2020/07/02/definition-of-chatzos/) on the KosherJava blog.\n\nChatzos is solar midnight, when the sun is at its lowest."
  description (flipped config): "Chatzos halayla.\n\nFor how chatzos can be defined and calculated, see [The Definition of Chatzos](https://kosherjava.com/2020/07/02/definition-of-chatzos/) on the KosherJava blog.\n\nChatzos is the midpoint between sea level sunset and the next sunrise."

getChatzosHayom
  name: Chatzos Hayom
  category: ChatzosHayom
  deprecated: false
  formula: ChatzosHayom
  description: "Chatzos hayom.\n\nFor how chatzos can be defined and calculated, see [The Definition of Chatzos](https://kosherjava.com/2020/07/02/definition-of-chatzos/) on the KosherJava blog.\n\nChatzos is solar noon, when the sun crosses the meridian."
  description (flipped config): "Chatzos hayom.\n\nFor how chatzos can be defined and calculated, see [The Definition of Chatzos](https://kosherjava.com/2020/07/02/definition-of-chatzos/) on the KosherJava blog.\n\nChatzos is the midpoint between sea level sunrise and sunset."

getChatzosHayomAsHalfDay
  name: Chatzos Hayom (Midpoint of Sunrise and Sunset)
  category: ChatzosHayom
  deprecated: false
  formula: ChatzosHayomAsHalfDay
  description: "Chatzos hayom calculated as the halfway point between sunrise and sunset.\n\nThis is the same as six shaos zmaniyos after sunrise when the day is measured from sunrise to sunset. Many hold that chatzos is the midpoint between sea level sunrise and sea level sunset, even though astronomical chatzos is usually a slightly different time.\n\nA day measured from alos to tzais with the same offset on both sides can also have the same midpoint.\n\nFor how chatzos can be defined and calculated, see [The Definition of Chatzos](https://kosherjava.com/2020/07/02/definition-of-chatzos/) on the KosherJava blog.\n\nIn places such as the Arctic Circle, where there is at least one day a year when the sun does not rise and one when it does not set, this zman may not be available or cannot be calculated."

getEndAstronomicalTwilight
  name: End Astronomical Twilight
  category: Twilight
  deprecated: false
  formula: EndAstronomicalTwilight
  description: "The end of astronomical twilight in the evening.\n\nCalculated using a zenith of 108 degrees.\n\nThis zman may not be available or cannot be calculated when the computation cannot be performed."

getEndCivilTwilight
  name: End Civil Twilight
  category: Twilight
  deprecated: false
  formula: EndCivilTwilight
  description: "The end of [civil twilight](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twilight#Civil_twilight) in the evening.\n\nCalculated using a zenith of 96 degrees.\n\nThis zman may not be available or cannot be calculated when the computation cannot be performed."

getEndNauticalTwilight
  name: End Nautical Twilight
  category: Twilight
  deprecated: false
  formula: EndNauticalTwilight
  description: "The end of nautical twilight in the evening.\n\nCalculated using a zenith of 102 degrees.\n\nThis zman may not be available or cannot be calculated when the computation cannot be performed."

getFixedLocalChatzosHayom
  name: Chatzos Hayom (Fixed Local Chatzos)
  category: ChatzosHayom
  deprecated: false
  formula: LocalMeanTime(12.0)
  description: "Fixed local chatzos - clock noon adjusted for the location's longitude and time zone, not tied only to theoretical 15-degree time zones.\n\nThe globe is divided into 24 hours over 360 degrees, or 15 degrees per hour (4 minutes per degree). At longitudes 0, 15, 30, and so on, chatzos is exactly 12:00 noon. The result is adjusted to the actual time zone and [daylight saving time](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daylight_saving_time).\n\nThis is the time of chatzos according to the [Aruch Hashulchan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aruch_HaShulchan) ([Orach Chaim 233:14](https://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=7705&pgnum=426)) and [Rabbi Moshe Feinstein](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moshe_Feinstein) ([Igros Moshe, Orach Chaim 1:24](https://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=916&st=&pgnum=67), [2:20](https://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=14675&pgnum=191))."

getMinchaGedola16Point1Degrees
  name: Mincha Gedola (16.1 Degrees)
  category: MinchaGedola
  deprecated: false
  formula: MinchaGedola(SunriseOffsetByDegrees(16.1), SunsetOffsetByDegrees(16.1), true)
  description: "Mincha gedola according to the Magen Avraham, using the 16.1-degree day.\n\nHalf a shaah zmanis after chatzos hayom, using a day that begins and ends at 16.1 degrees.\n\nAt some northern and southern locations, this zman may not be available if the sun does not reach low enough below the horizon.\n\nEach shaah zmanis is a twelfth of the whole day."
  description (flipped config): "Mincha gedola according to the Magen Avraham, using the 16.1-degree day.\n\nHalf a shaah zmanis after chatzos hayom, using a day that begins and ends at 16.1 degrees.\n\nAt some northern and southern locations, this zman may not be available if the sun does not reach low enough below the horizon.\n\nEach shaah zmanis is a sixth of the afternoon, from chatzos to the end of the day.\n\nChatzos is the midpoint between sea level sunrise and sunset."

getMinchaGedola30Minutes
  name: Mincha Gedola (30 Minutes)
  category: MinchaGedola
  deprecated: false
  formula: Offset(ChatzosHayom, 30m)
  description: "Mincha gedola calculated as 30 minutes after chatzos hayom.\n\nSome use this in winter when half a shaah zmanis is less than 30 minutes, to delay the start of mincha.\n\nDo not use this time to begin mincha before standard mincha gedola GRA.\n\nIn places where chatzos cannot be calculated, this zman may not be available.\n\nChatzos is solar noon, when the sun crosses the meridian."
  description (flipped config): "Mincha gedola calculated as 30 minutes after chatzos hayom.\n\nSome use this in winter when half a shaah zmanis is less than 30 minutes, to delay the start of mincha.\n\nDo not use this time to begin mincha before standard mincha gedola GRA.\n\nIn places where chatzos cannot be calculated, this zman may not be available.\n\nChatzos is the midpoint between sea level sunrise and sunset."

getMinchaGedola72Minutes
  name: Mincha Gedola (72 Minutes)
  category: MinchaGedola
  deprecated: false
  formula: MinchaGedola(Offset(ConfiguredSunrise, 1h 12m ago), Offset(ConfiguredSunset, 1h 12m), true)
  description: "Mincha gedola according to the Magen Avraham.\n\nHalf a shaah zmanis after chatzos hayom, using a day from alos 72 minutes to tzais 72 minutes.\n\nIn places where sunrise or sunset cannot be calculated, this zman may not be available.\n\nThis zman is calculated as though the configured location were at sea level.\n\nEach shaah zmanis is a twelfth of the whole day."
  description (flipped config): "Mincha gedola according to the Magen Avraham.\n\nHalf a shaah zmanis after chatzos hayom, using a day from alos 72 minutes to tzais 72 minutes.\n\nIn places where sunrise or sunset cannot be calculated, this zman may not be available.\n\nThis zman takes the configured location's elevation into account when it is calculated.\n\nEach shaah zmanis is a sixth of the afternoon, from chatzos to the end of the day.\n\nChatzos is the midpoint between sea level sunrise and sunset."

getMinchaGedolaAhavatShalom
  name: Mincha Gedola (Ahavat Shalom)
  category: MinchaGedola
  deprecated: false
  formula: MinchaGedolaAhavatShalom
  description: "Mincha gedola according to Rabbi Yaakov Moshe Hillel, as published in the luach of the Bais Horaah of Yeshivat Chevrat Ahavat Shalom.\n\nHalf a shaah zmanis after chatzos, using a day from alos 16.1 degrees to tzais 3.7 degrees.\n\nThe later of this time or 30 clock minutes after chatzos is used.\n\nAt some northern and southern locations, this zman may not be available if the sun does not reach low enough below the horizon.\n\nChatzos is solar noon, when the sun crosses the meridian."
  description (flipped config): "Mincha gedola according to Rabbi Yaakov Moshe Hillel, as published in the luach of the Bais Horaah of Yeshivat Chevrat Ahavat Shalom.\n\nHalf a shaah zmanis after chatzos, using a day from alos 16.1 degrees to tzais 3.7 degrees.\n\nThe later of this time or 30 clock minutes after chatzos is used.\n\nAt some northern and southern locations, this zman may not be available if the sun does not reach low enough below the horizon.\n\nChatzos is the midpoint between sea level sunrise and sunset."

getMinchaGedolaAteretTorah
  name: Mincha Gedola (Ateret Torah)
  category: MinchaGedola
  deprecated: false
  formula: MinchaGedola(ZmanisOffset(ConfiguredSunrise, -1.2), TzaisAteretTorah, false)
  description: "Mincha gedola according to the Ateret Torah calculation of Chacham Yosef Harari-Raful of Yeshivat Ateret Torah.\n\n6.5 shaos zmaniyos after alos.\n\nThe day begins at alos 1/10 of the day before sunrise and ends 40 minutes after sunset.\n\nIn places where sunrise or sunset cannot be calculated, this zman may not be available.\n\nThis zman is calculated as though the configured location were at sea level."
  description (flipped config): "Mincha gedola according to the Ateret Torah calculation of Chacham Yosef Harari-Raful of Yeshivat Ateret Torah.\n\n6.5 shaos zmaniyos after alos.\n\nThe day begins at alos 1/10 of the day before sunrise and ends 25 minutes after sunset.\n\nIn places where sunrise or sunset cannot be calculated, this zman may not be available.\n\nThis zman takes the configured location's elevation into account when it is calculated."

getMinchaGedolaBaalHatanya
  name: Mincha Gedola (Baal Hatanya)
  category: MinchaGedola
  deprecated: false
  formula: MinchaGedola(SunriseOffsetByDegrees(1.583), SunsetOffsetByDegrees(1.583), true)
  description: "Mincha gedola according to the Baal Hatanya.\n\n6.5 shaos zmaniyos after netz amiti, using a day from Baal Hatanya sunrise to sunset.\n\nIn places where sunrise or sunset cannot be calculated, this zman may not be available.\n\nEach shaah zmanis is a twelfth of the whole day."
  description (flipped config): "Mincha gedola according to the Baal Hatanya.\n\n6.5 shaos zmaniyos after netz amiti, using a day from Baal Hatanya sunrise to sunset.\n\nIn places where sunrise or sunset cannot be calculated, this zman may not be available.\n\nEach shaah zmanis is a sixth of the afternoon, from chatzos to the end of the day.\n\nChatzos is the midpoint between sea level sunrise and sunset."

getMinchaGedolaGRA
  name: Mincha Gedola (GR'A)
  category: MinchaGedola
  deprecated: false
  formula: MinchaGedola(ConfiguredSunrise, ConfiguredSunset, true)
  description: "Mincha gedola according to the [Vilna Gaon](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vilna_Gaon).\n\n6.5 shaos zmaniyos after sunrise. The day is measured from sunrise to sunset for the proportional hour.\n\nThis is the earliest time one can pray mincha.\n\nIn places where sunrise or sunset cannot be calculated, this zman may not be available.\n\nThis zman is calculated as though the configured location were at sea level.\n\nEach shaah zmanis is a twelfth of the whole day."
  description (flipped config): "Mincha gedola according to the [Vilna Gaon](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vilna_Gaon).\n\n6.5 shaos zmaniyos after sunrise. The day is measured from sunrise to sunset for the proportional hour.\n\nThis is the earliest time one can pray mincha.\n\nIn places where sunrise or sunset cannot be calculated, this zman may not be available.\n\nThis zman takes the configured location's elevation into account when it is calculated.\n\nEach shaah zmanis is a sixth of the afternoon, from chatzos to the end of the day.\n\nChatzos is the midpoint between sea level sunrise and sunset."

getMinchaGedolaGRAFixedLocalChatzos30Minutes
  name: Mincha Gedola (GR'A, Fixed Local Chatzos, 30 Minutes)
